{
  "title": "Namaz of Imam al-Askari (a.s.)",
  "data": "Upon concluding the prayer, say the following supplication:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَسْاَلُكَ بِاَنَّ لَكَ الْحَمْدَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUKA BI-ANNA LAKAL HAMD\nO Allah, I beseech You in the name of all praise being to You;\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANT\nthere is no god save You,\nالْبَدِيْءُ قَبْلَ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ\nAL-BADEE'U QABLA KULLI SHAY'\n[You are] the Premier before all things;\nوَاَنْتَ الْحَيُّ الْقَيُّوْمُ\nWA ANTAL HAYYUL QAYYOOM\nand You are the Ever-living, the Self-Subsistent;\nوَلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ\nWA LAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANT\nand there is no god save You,\nالَّذِيْ لَا يُذِلُّكَ شَيْءٌ\nALLADHEE LAA YUDHILLUKA SHAY'\nnothing can humiliate You;\nوَاَنْتَ كُلَّ يَوْمٍ فِيْ شَاْنٍ\nWA ANTA KULLA YAWMIN FEE SHA'N\nand You, every moment, are in a state (of glory).\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANT\nThere is no god save You,\nخَالِقُ مَا يُرٰى وَمَا لَا يُرٰى\nKHAALIQU MAA YURAA WA MAA LAA YURAA\nthe Creator of what is seen and what cannot be seen,\nالْعَالِمُ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ بِغَيْرِ تَعْلِيْمٍ\nAL-A'ALIMU BIKULLI SHAY'IN BIGHAYRI TA'LEEM\nthe Knower of all things without learning;\nاَسْاَلُكَ بِآلَائِكَ وَنَعْمَائِكَ\nAS'ALUKA BI-AALAA'IKA WA NA'MAA'IK\nI beseech You in the name of Your bounties and gratuities\nبِاَنَّكَ اللّٰهُ الرَّبُّ الْوَاحِدُ\nBI-ANNAKAL LAAHUR RABBUL WAAHID\nand in the name of Your being Allah, the One Lord,\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANT\nthere is no god save You,\nالرَّحْمٰنُ الرَّحِيْمُ\nAR-RAHMAANUR RAHEEM\nthe All-beneficent, the All-merciful;\nوَاَسْاَلُكَ بِاَنَّكَ اَنْتَ اللّٰهُ\nWA AS'ALUKA BI-ANNAKA ANTALLAAH\nand I beseech You in the name of Your being Allah;\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANT\nthere is no god save You,\nالْوِتْرُ الْفَرْدُ\nAL-WITRUL FARD\nthe Unique, the Single,\nالْاَحَدُ الصَّمَدُ\nAL-AHADUS SAMAD\nthe One, and the eternally Besought of all,\nالَّذِيْ لَمْ يَلِدْ وَلَمْ يُوْلَدْ\nALLADHEE LAM YALID WA LAM YOOLAD\nWho begets not, nor is he begotten,\nوَلَمْ يَكُنْ لَهٗ كُفُواً اَحَدٌ\nWA LAM YAKUN LAHOO KUFUWAN AHAD\nand none is like Him.\nوَاَسْاَلُكَ بِاَنَّكَ اللّٰهُ\nWA AS'ALUKA BI-ANNAKALLAAH\nAnd I beseech You in the name of Your being Allah,\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANT\nthere is no god save You;\nاللَّطِيْفُ الْخَبِيْرُ\nAL-LATEEFUL KHABEER\nthe Knower of subtleties, the All-aware,\nالْقَائِمُ عَلٰى كُلِّ نَفْسٍ بِمَا كَسَبَتْ\nAL-QAA'IMU A'LAA KULLI NAFSIN BIMAA KASABAT\nWho watches every soul as to what it earns,\nالرَّقِيْبُ الْحَفِيْظُ\nAR-RAQEEBUL HAFEEZ\nthe Watcher, the Preserver.\nوَاَسْاَلُكَ بِاَنَّكَ اللّٰهُ\nWA AS'ALUKA BI-ANNAKALLAAH\nAnd I beseech You in the name of Your being Allah,\nالْاَوَّلُ قَبْلَ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ\nAL-AWWALU QABLA KULLI SHAY'\nthe First before all things,\nوَالآخِرُ بَعْدَ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ\nWAL AAKHIRU BA'DA KULLI SHAY'\nthe Last after all things,\nوَالْبَاطِنُ دُوْنَ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ\nWAL BAATINU DOONA KULLI SHAY'\nthe Knower of all hidden things,\nالضَّارُّ النَّافِعُ\nAD-DAARRUN NAAFI'\nthe source of both harm [for those who deserve harm] and benefit,\nالْحَكِيْمُ الْعَلِيْمُ\nAL-HAKEEMUL A'LEEM\nthe All-wise, and All-knowing.\nوَاَسْاَلُكَ بِاَنَّكَ اَنْتَ اللّٰهُ\nWA AS'ALUKA BI-ANNAKA ANTALLAAH\nAnd I beseech You in the name of Your being Allah,\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANT\nthere is no god save You,\nالْحَيُّ الْقَيُّوْمُ\nAL-HAYYUL QAYYOOM\nthe Ever-living, the Self-Subsistent,\nالْبَاعِثُ الْوَارِثُ\nAL-BAA'ITHUL WAARITH\nthe Resurrector, the Inheritor,\nالْحَنَّانُ الْمَنَّانُ\nAL-HANNAANUL MANNAAN\nthe All-tender, the All-favorer,\nبَدِيْعُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْاَرْضِ\nBADEE'US SAMAAWAATI WAL ARD\nthe Fashioner of the heavens and the earth,\nذُوْ الْجَلَالِ وَالْاِكْرَامِ\nDHUL JALAALI WAL IKRAAM\nthe Lord of majesty and honor,\nوَذُوْ الطَّوْلِ وَذُوْ الْعِزَّةِ وَذُوْ السُّلْطَانِ\nWA DHUT TAWLI WA DHUL I'ZZATI WA DHUS SULTAAN\nand the Lord of bounty, dignity, and absolute authority.\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANT\nThere is no god save You;\nاَحَطْتَ بِكُلِّ شَيْءٍ عِلْماً\nAHATTA BIKULLI SHAY'IN I'LMAA\nYou encompass all things with knowledge,\nوَاَحْصَيْتَ كُلَّ شَيْءٍ عَدَداً\nWA AHSAYTA KULLA SHAY'IN A'DADAA\nand You record the number of all things;\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\n(please) send blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad.",
  "merits": "In his book of Jamal al-Usbu', Sayyid Ibn Tawus has recorded a special prayer and supplication for each of the Holy Imams (a.s.), to be offered on Fridays.\nImam al-Askari (a.s.)'s prayer consists of four units. In each of the first two units, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Zalzalah](A103) fifteen times; in each of the last two, [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) fifteen times."
}
